  "flows": [
    { "id": "hbm-to-iod-left", "from": "hbm-dram-left", "to": "iod-left", "group": "memory", "particles": 2 },
    { "id": "hbm-to-iod-right", "from": "hbm-dram-right", "to": "iod-right", "group": "memory", "particles": 2 },
    { "id": "iod-to-iod", "from": "iod-left", "to": "iod-right", "group": "io", "particles": 3 },
    { "id": "iod-to-xcd-left", "from": "iod-left", "to": "xcd-left", "group": "compute", "particles": 2 },
    { "id": "iod-to-xcd-right", "from": "iod-right", "to": "xcd-right", "group": "compute", "particles": 2 }
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "1. Weights W and activations X sit in the 288 GB HBM3E pool (8 stacks, 12-Hi).",
      "focus": ["hbm-dram-left", "hbm-dram-right", "hbm-base-left", "hbm-base-right"],
      "dot": "hbm-dram-left",
      "explode": 0.6,
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "hbm"
    },
    {
      "text": "2. The local IOD's memory controller reads the 4 HBM3E stacks next to it.",
      "focus": ["mc-left"],
      "dot": "mc-left",
      "stage": "memory-controller"
    },
    {
      "text": "3. If the tile lives on the other IOD's HBM, it crosses the on-package Infinity Fabric link between the 2 IODs (at most 1 hop, vs up to 2 on MI300X's 4-IOD layout).",
      "focus": ["ifab-link"],
      "dot": "ifab-link",
      "stage": "die-to-die"
    },
    {
      "text": "4. Data lands in the 256 MB Infinity Cache, shared by all 8 XCDs over the fabric.",
      "focus": ["infinity-cache-left"],
      "dot": "infinity-cache-left",
      "stage": "infinity-cache"
    },
    {
      "text": "5. The owning XCD pulls the tile into its local, shared L2 cache.",
      "focus": ["l2-xcd"],
      "dot": "l2-xcd",
      "drill": "xcd-detail",
      "stage": "l2"
    },
    {
      "text": "6. A Compute Unit copies A/B tiles from L2 into its 160 KB Local Data Share (LDS).",
      "focus": ["lds"],
      "dot": "lds",
      "drill": "cu-detail",
      "stage": "shared-memory"
    },
    {
      "text": "7. The CU issues an MFMA instruction: its 4 Matrix Cores multiply the tiles, e.g. in MXFP4.",
      "focus": ["matrix-core"],
      "dot": "matrix-core",
      "drill": "cu-detail",
      "stage": "tensor-core"
    },
    {
      "text": "8. Partial sums accumulate in the dedicated AccVGPR accumulator registers, not the general VGPRs. Steps 6-8 repeat along K.",
      "focus": ["accumulator"],
      "dot": "accumulator",
      "drill": "cu-detail",
      "stage": "accumulate"
    },
    {
      "text": "9. Epilogue: results move AccVGPR -> VGPR; scalar/vector ALUs add bias, apply activation, quantize.",
      "focus": ["vgpr", "scalar-alu"],
      "dot": "vgpr",
      "drill": "cu-detail",
      "stage": "epilogue"
    },
    {
      "text": "10. Results flow back L2 -> Infinity Cache -> HBM3E; across GPUs, Infinity Fabric (7 links x 153 GB/s) all-reduces the result.",
      "focus": ["ifab-link"],
      "dot": "ifab-link",
      "drill": null,
      "stage": "writeback"
    }
  ],
